node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRSysYA","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T17:15:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T17:15:53Z","body":"All popup backgrounds became so dark in 4.6 because they needed to get enough contrast against the base editor color underneath them (people wanted popups not to blend in with the editor). Color picker also has this problem. There are 2 solutions:\n\n1. Temporary solution: Just change the color of *some* popups to be brighter where the content is complex, like the environment settings and the color picker. This will hurt the visibility of the popup boundaries but improve the visibility of UI elements inside of it.\n2. Proper solution: Add shadows to popups to make it possible to make their backgrounds same color as editor base color. This will require either [enabling per-pixel transparency](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324) for editor windows, or, better yet, [embedding them](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3204396046) like blender does.\n\nEmbedding would be great not only because it will allow shadows, it will also allow rounded corners which are necessary to make them fit the theme aesthetically. It was briefly discussed last year internally during the theme port, but nobody got around to implementing that yet","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5455522912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5455543684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122215#issuecomment-5455543684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122215","id":5455543684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRSz9hA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T17:17:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T17:17:59Z","body":"Popups aren't the only place where this is a problem, see #122882.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5455543684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5455768808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122215#issuecomment-5455768808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122215","id":5455768808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRTBs6A","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T17:40:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T17:40:28Z","body":"Ah my bad I didn't realize that the issue is about those buttons specifically.\n\nI don't think it makes sense to use accent color in all buttons on click, in the classic theme it introduced a lot of noise. So there are 2 solutions for those buttons:\n\n1. A type variation for those cases where regular non-flat buttons are used as toggles to add accent color to them\n2. Stick to `CheckBox`/`CheckButton` for those\n\nThe second option seems better because there are very few places in godot editor where regular buttons are used as toggles, so it currently doesn't make sense to have them as a category from the UX perspective\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5455768808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]